=== CURRENT WORK ===

Touch panels, the guided setup (plan approved 2026-10-31, `~/.claude/plans/sleepy-roaming-kahn.md`): method 1 (automatic: the output's turn and mirror applied to the panel) and the
manual orientation of a separate panel are DONE and verified on the real panel of Pi A. Still to build, in this order: (2) mapping by touching the four corners, (3) calibration by exact
points, and the simple guided web UI ("Touch doesn't match? Fix it" dialog, totem overlay built inert, "Try it" step, API `start_setup/confirm_setup/cancel_setup/reset`, events
`Settings/Display/Touch/setup`, `SetTouchSetup`). The raw events are read from `/dev/input/eventN` in the node; nothing is saved before the visitor says the dot follows the finger.

=== OPEN (history: docs/TODO-archive.md; what each thing is: CLAUDE.md) ===

--- To build (mine) ---
* Touch guided setup, see CURRENT WORK.
* Drag and drop of a link or a file onto a page must not navigate the window away (CEF drag handler; the window already undoes a navigation away, this stops it earlier).
* Remote control: adopting a client that has its own window layouts, and unpairing one that has panes (its layouts are dropped, what they showed stays on the server); per-window
  settings (audio output, keyboard, language, screensaver, refresh) do not travel with the playlists on adoption.
* Notifications: dismissal is global (per user would be better); a manual suspend refusal does not raise one; a pairing-request notification can stay stale until the next change.
* PDF: remote viewers (a client needs the file and its own /pdf-view), fonts that are not embedded, pages larger than 4096 px.
* Playlist page: drag-and-drop reorder with two playlists was never exercised in a browser (tools/ui-playlists.py covers create/switch/rename).
* Command confirmations ("Show confirmation on command execution", BACKLOG).
* The "first frame drawn" line was seen twice for one window on a Pi (2026-10-16): check that a page is not attached by two DevTools sessions.
* Display power by GPIO (idea).

--- Waiting for the user (decisions and things only they can see) ---
* Long press on the real panel: no context menu should appear (Pi A, dev code mounted; needs the user's finger).
* Remote control: is TCP 4443 acceptable on the image (firewall)?
* H.264/AAC: the build ships the proprietary codecs (user rule); the patent/licensing question moves to whoever distributes the image (VM-TESTING.md 8b), not a technical decision.
* Open the upstream pull requests for CEF and cefpython (docs/cef-wayland/pr-cef.md, pr-cefpython.md)?
* Pointer cursor policy of the viewer windows.

--- Waiting for unitotem-system (image) or for the next deb set ---
* dev19 debs: everything since dev18 (touch name fix, inert pages, screen-off fix, names hardening, lockdown, developer tools, language per window, locale paks, profile
  preferences, labwc rc.xml without default keybinds, hotspot fix). Build when the user or the system session says; cefpython is unchanged.
* `/etc/chromium.d/50-unitotem-accel` is still in the image and configures a browser that is not installed (the viewer sets its switches itself).
* Identity merge at OTA (`migrate-etc-overlay`): accounts and root's password across a slot switch, verify with a real A/B cycle; the browser profile (cookies) across a slot switch.
* A session bus for root so GUI applications reach the notification daemon; `unitotem-boot-orientation` installed on boards (Plymouth turned); the new `rc.xml` (Alt+F4 etc.).
* Mixed versions (old viewer with a new manager and the reverse) and rollback to the previous slot with a turned screen were reasoned, never run.

--- Needs hardware or a setup I do not have ---
* CEC (no adapter), serial power commands (no port), Wake-on-LAN of a monitor with a NIC, DDC writes on monitors other than the LG and the Realtek board.
* A client (remote) viewer's pixels, the approval click path in the UI, behind a firewall that blocks 4443, multi-GB transfers.
* Camera and microphone: `getUserMedia` answers `NotFoundError` on the boards (they have neither); a real capture was never seen.
* Real playback checks left in VM-TESTING.md section 7; per-asset volume and per-window audio output have been checked on a Pi with the capture card, not on a remote viewer.

--- Closed, so nobody asks again ---
Superseded entries of the old log: the welcome screen on a genuine first boot, the last screen going unnoticed, the scrollbar on the welcome page, the codecs, the interim per-window ticker store
(`WindowLayout.ticker` is the store), Updates page against the real updater (checked on the boards), timers and screens, VNC, suspend, PAM accounts, first access, notification center,
Wayland, rotation by the compositor, cookies, the keyboard, the network drops (2026-10-31), the lean CEF build (measured, not worth it: docs/cef-lean-build.md).

